Mingla #2107: backport of expo/expo#43937 ("iOS | SharedObjectRegistry: Fix
crash when reloading javascript", merged upstream 2026-03-18 as 7d7ad101c).

SharedObjectRegistry used a DispatchQueue whose async clear()/delete() freed JS
weak objects on a background queue after Updates.reloadAsync() had torn the JS
runtime down: use-after-free in -[EXJavaScriptWeakObject .cxx_destruct]. This
swaps the queue for an NSLock so clear() and delete() free on the calling
thread. Adapted to 3.0.30: explicit lock()/unlock() (NSLock.withLock needs
iOS 16; the pod targets 15.1), and the lock is never held while native objects
are released, release callbacks run, or a JS weak object is locked, so nothing
that re-enters the registry can deadlock.

NATIVE-ONLY (a Swift pod source file). It takes effect only in the NEXT store
build; an OTA cannot ship it. The JS mitigation (release every expo-video player
before reloadAsync) covers builds already in the stores.

REMOVE this patch when Mingla moves to Expo SDK 55+ (expo-modules-core with the
upstream fix). The same patch lives in app-mobile/patches and
mingla-business/patches; keep both identical.

